{
  "about": [
    "Budgets of tools/perf/budget.mjs, per source: Windows' --smooth-check at each placement (ci.yml, job smooth), the Mac's (mac.yml), Mira for Windows at rest (tools/idle-check.ps1, ci.yml job build).",
    "Set on 2026-11-07 from 6 runs of ci.yml (main and pull requests, 2026-11-06, runner windows-2025, 4 processors, WARP, 1024 x 768, 64 Hz) and 4 of mac.yml (macos-15, 3 processors, about 38 Hz; a fifth at 10 Hz left out).",
    "iPhone (testOpening on ios.yml's simulator, 6 runs of 2026-11-06, the stand-in Jellyfin slow by 1.5 s): launch to Home 7.5-10.4 s, of which 1.4-2.1 s after XCTest's launch returned; Jellyfin away, launch to Home 7.2-9.4 s. Opening.swift then gave up at 3 s with Home kept and 12 s without; since 2026-11-07 it waits for Jellyfin even with Home kept, 15 s at most.",
    "Windows measured then: scrolling 71-92 % of the refreshes shown; the interface thread held at most 49 ms opening Films the first time, 22 ms Séries, 36 ms Films again, 54 ms a title's page, 34 ms closing it, 76 ms Réglages, 4 ms closing them, 35 ms back to Accueil; a scroll's frame at most 21 ms (a GC). Mac's clicks: Films 1st 21-52 ms (93 at 10 Hz), Séries 3-17, Films 2nd 2-20, title 24-30, back 13-24, Réglages 98-218, Accueil 5-9. At rest: 0-3.4 % of a core (0.13 % but once), 82-93 MB, 0 bytes written.",
    "A fail sits at 2 to 4 times the worst measured, a warning near it: a fail is a step back no runner's noise makes, measured twice. Shown is the share of the screen's refreshes that got a frame; Held the longest the interface's thread was held (Windows: a frame's work or another operation); Click the Mac's own work on a click.",
    "Change a budget only with the numbers that justify it, in this note; a phase renamed in a check must be renamed here (a missing phase fails)."
  ],
